# Integrations

External systems are reached only through ports and adapters. Domain code depends on ports, not vendor SDKs.

Webhook signatures, replay rejection, GitHub installation mapping, credential encryption, SBOM URL non-fetch, and intelligence overwrite policy are canonical in [security.mdc](security.mdc). They apply even when the handler lives in `apps/api` or `apps/worker`.

## Adapters

- Treat feed payloads, package metadata, and remote API responses as untrusted. Validate with Zod at the adapter boundary.
- Consider malicious package metadata and dependency compromise. Do not execute URLs from SBOM or feed fields.
- Object storage is provider-neutral. Local development may use MinIO. Handlers and domain code must not call storage SDKs directly.
- Development adapters (unsigned webhooks, plaintext credential stubs, unrestricted HTTP) must not be selectable in production config.

## Claims

- Do not assert exploitability, KEV applicability, or remediation solely because a feed mentioned a CVE. Record evidence and the matching method.
